{"family":"qb-a12-ma-s3","course":"ADV","year":12,"topic":"MA-S3","questions":[{"id":"A12-S3-007","group":"A12-S3-007","dp":"S3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Finding the mean","prompt":"A normally distributed variable has standard deviation $5$, and $2.5\\%$ of values exceed $80$. Use the empirical rule to find the mean.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":70},"hints":["95% lie within 2 SD.","Each tail is 2.5%.","Solve for μ."],"ladder":{"nudge":"95% lie within 2 SD.","method":"Each tail is 2.5%.","worked":"Solve for μ."},"steps":[{"h":"Rule","d":"2.5% above is 2 SD above the mean: $\\mu+10=80$"}],"traps":[{"value":75,"why":"Used 1 SD."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"80 is μ + 2σ","line":"mu+2*5 = 80"},{"marks":1,"point":"μ = 70","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-012","group":"A12-S3-012","dp":"S3.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Rejected bolts","prompt":"Bolt lengths are normally distributed with mean $20$ mm and standard deviation $0.2$ mm. Bolts shorter than $19.6$ mm or longer than $20.4$ mm are rejected. Estimate how many of a batch of $2000$ are rejected.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":100},"hints":["Convert the limits to z.","95% within 2 SD.","Multiply by 2000."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Convert the limits to z.","method":"95% within 2 SD.","worked":"Multiply by 2000."},"steps":[{"h":"z","d":"$19.6,20.4$ are $\\pm2$ SD; 5% rejected"},{"h":"Count","d":"$0.05\\times2000=100$"}],"traps":[{"value":1900,"why":"That is the number accepted."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"5% outside ±2σ","line":"0.05*2000"},{"marks":1,"point":"About 100","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-014","group":"A12-S3-014","dp":"S3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Lower tail band","prompt":"Exam marks for $400$ students are normally distributed. Use the empirical rule to estimate how many scored between $3$ standard deviations and $1$ standard deviation below the mean.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":63},"hints":["Half of 99.7%.","Subtract half of 68%.","Multiply by 400."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Half of 99.7%.","method":"Subtract half of 68%.","worked":"$49.85\\%-34\\%=15.85\\%$"},"steps":[{"h":"Rule","d":"$49.85\\%-34\\%=15.85\\%$"},{"h":"Count","d":"$0.1585\\times400\\approx63$"}],"traps":[{"value":54,"why":"Used 47.5% − 34% (2 SD, not 3)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"15.85%","line":"0.1585*400"},{"marks":1,"point":"About 63","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-016(i)","group":"A12-S3-016","label":"(i)","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Density proportional to x squared","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=kx^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le3$.\n\nFind $k$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.1111111111111111},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Total probability is 1.","Integrate kx².","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total probability is 1.","method":"Integrate kx².","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Total area","d":"$9k=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.3333333333333333,"why":"Integral of x² from 0 to 3 is 9.","expr":"1/3"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1/9","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-016(ii)","group":"A12-S3-016","label":"(ii)","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Density proportional to x squared","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=kx^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le3$.\n\nFind $P(X>2)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.7037037037037037},"hints":["Integrate from 2 to 3.","Use k = 1/9.","Simplify."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate from 2 to 3.","method":"Use k = 1/9.","worked":"Simplify."},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\tfrac19\\left[\\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}\\right]_2^3=\\tfrac{27-8}{27}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.2962962962962963,"why":"That is P(X < 2).","expr":"8/27"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct integral","line":"(27-8)/27"},{"marks":1,"point":"19/27","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-018","group":"A12-S3-018","dp":"S3.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"A z-score","prompt":"$X$ is normally distributed with mean $65$ and standard deviation $5$. Find the $z$-score of $72$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":1.4},"answerPrefix":"z =","hints":["z = (x − μ)/σ.","Subtract the mean.","Divide by 5."],"ladder":{"nudge":"z = (x − μ)/σ.","method":"Subtract the mean.","worked":"Divide by 5."},"steps":[{"h":"Standardise","d":"$\\tfrac{72-65}{5}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.71,"why":"Divided by 72 − 65 instead of σ."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1.4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-019","group":"A12-S3-019","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Symmetric interval about zero","prompt":"Given $P(Z<1.5)=0.9332$, find $P(-1.5<Z<1.5)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.8664},"hints":["Find one tail.","Both tails are equal.","Subtract from 1."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Find one tail.","method":"Both tails are equal.","worked":"Subtract from 1."},"steps":[{"h":"Tail","d":"$P(Z>1.5)=0.0668$"},{"h":"Middle","d":"$1-2(0.0668)=0.8664$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.9332,"why":"That is only P(Z < 1.5)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Tail 0.0668","line":"1-0.9332"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.8664","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-020","group":"A12-S3-020","dp":"S3.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Long-lasting batteries","prompt":"Battery lifetimes are normally distributed with mean $400$ hours and standard deviation $25$ hours. Use the empirical rule to estimate the percentage lasting more than $450$ hours.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2.5},"hints":["Standardise 450.","95% lie within 2 SD.","Halve the rest."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Standardise 450.","method":"95% lie within 2 SD.","worked":"$\\tfrac{450-400}{25}=2$"},"steps":[{"h":"z-score","d":"$\\tfrac{450-400}{25}=2$"},{"h":"Tail","d":"$\\tfrac{100-95}{2}=2.5\\%$"}],"traps":[{"value":5,"why":"Both tails together are 5%."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = 2","line":"z = 2"},{"marks":1,"point":"2.5%","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-022","group":"A12-S3-022","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Median of a linear density","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=2x$ for $0\\le x\\le1$. Find the exact median.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.7071067811865476},"answerPrefix":"m =","hints":["Integrate 2x from 0 to m.","Set equal to ½.","Take the positive root."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate 2x from 0 to m.","method":"Set equal to ½.","worked":"$m^{2}=\\tfrac12$"},"steps":[{"h":"Area to m","d":"$m^{2}=\\tfrac12$"},{"h":"Positive root","d":"$m=\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"The density is not uniform.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"m² = ½","line":"m^2 = 1/2"},{"marks":1,"point":"1/√2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-023","group":"A12-S3-023","dp":"S3.2b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Top five percent","prompt":"Exam scores are $N(80,6^{2})$. Given $P(Z<1.645)=0.95$, find the score above which the top $5\\%$ lie, to two decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":89.87,"tol":0.005},"hints":["Top 5% means P(X < x) = 0.95.","z = 1.645.","x = μ + zσ."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Top 5% means P(X < x) = 0.95.","method":"z = 1.645.","worked":"x = μ + zσ."},"steps":[{"h":"Unstandardise","d":"$80+1.645\\times6=89.87$"}],"traps":[{"value":70.13,"why":"That is the bottom 5% cut-off."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x = μ + 1.645σ","line":"80+1.645*6"},{"marks":1,"point":"89.87","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-025","group":"A12-S3-025","dp":"S3.1b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Exponential cumulative function","prompt":"The cumulative distribution function of $X$ is $F(x)=1-e^{-x/2}$ for $x\\ge0$. Find the exact value of $P(1<X<3)$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"e^(-1/2)-e^(-3/2)"},"hints":["Use F(b) − F(a).","Substitute 3 and 1.","The 1s cancel."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Use F(b) − F(a).","method":"Substitute 3 and 1.","worked":"The 1s cancel."},"steps":[{"h":"Difference","d":"$F(3)-F(1)=\\left(1-e^{-3/2}\\right)-\\left(1-e^{-1/2}\\right)$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"e^(-3/2)-e^(-1/2)","why":"Subtracted in the wrong order."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"F(3) − F(1)","line":"(1-e^(-3/2))-(1-e^(-1/2))"},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-027","group":"A12-S3-027","dp":"S3.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Symmetric middle probability","prompt":"For a normal variable, $P(X<\\mu-a)=0.2$. Find $P(\\mu-a<X<\\mu+a)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.6},"hints":["The upper tail is also 0.2.","Subtract both tails.","Use symmetry."],"ladder":{"nudge":"The upper tail is also 0.2.","method":"Subtract both tails.","worked":"Use symmetry."},"steps":[{"h":"Symmetry","d":"$1-2(0.2)=0.6$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.8,"why":"Only removed one tail."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-029","group":"A12-S3-029","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Eightieth percentile of heights","prompt":"Heights are $N(170,10^{2})$ cm. Given $P(Z<0.84)\\approx0.8$, estimate the $80$th percentile.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":178.4,"tol":0.05},"hints":["Find z for 0.8.","x = μ + zσ.","Substitute."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Find z for 0.8.","method":"x = μ + zσ.","worked":"Substitute."},"steps":[{"h":"Unstandardise","d":"$170+0.84\\times10$"}],"traps":[{"value":161.6,"why":"That is the 20th percentile."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"178.4 cm","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-030","group":"A12-S3-030","dp":"S3.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Exponential density on a short interval","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=ke^{-x}$ for $0\\le x\\le\\ln4$. Find $k$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":1.3333333333333333},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Total area is 1.","e^{−ln 4} = ¼.","Solve for k."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total area is 1.","method":"e^{−ln 4} = ¼.","worked":"Solve for k."},"steps":[{"h":"Area","d":"$k\\left[-e^{-x}\\right]_0^{\\ln4}=k\\left(1-\\tfrac14\\right)=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":1,"why":"The interval is not [0, ∞)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"¾k = 1","line":"3/4*k = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"4/3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-031","group":"A12-S3-031","dp":"S3.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Lower tail of a quadratic density","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=\\tfrac38x^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le2$. Find $P(X<1)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.125},"hints":["Integrate f from 0 to 1.","Primitive x³/8.","Evaluate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate f from 0 to 1.","method":"Primitive x³/8.","worked":"Evaluate."},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\left[\\tfrac{x^{3}}{8}\\right]_0^1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"The density is not uniform.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1/8","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-032","group":"A12-S3-032","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Constant for a quadratic density","prompt":"Find $k$ so that $f(x)=k\\left(4-x^{2}\\right)$ for $0\\le x\\le2$ is a probability density function.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.1875},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Total area 1.","Integrate 4 − x².","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total area 1.","method":"Integrate 4 − x².","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Area","d":"$k\\left[4x-\\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}\\right]_0^2=\\tfrac{16k}{3}=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.125,"why":"Integrated 4 − x² as 8.","expr":"1/8"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Integral 16k/3","line":"16*k/3 = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"3/16","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-033","group":"A12-S3-033","dp":"S3.1c","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Uniform probability","prompt":"$X$ is uniformly distributed on $2\\le x\\le8$. Find $P(3<X<5)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3333333333333333},"hints":["Density is 1/6.","Length of the interval is 2.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Density is 1/6.","method":"Length of the interval is 2.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"Proportion","d":"$\\tfrac{5-3}{8-2}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.25,"why":"Divided by 8.","expr":"1/4"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1/3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-034","group":"A12-S3-034","dp":"S3.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"From one SD below to two above","prompt":"For a normal distribution, use the empirical rule to find the percentage of values between $\\mu-\\sigma$ and $\\mu+2\\sigma$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":81.5},"hints":["Half of 68% on the left.","Half of 95% on the right.","Add."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Half of 68% on the left.","method":"Half of 95% on the right.","worked":"Add."},"steps":[{"h":"Add halves","d":"$34+47.5$"}],"traps":[{"value":95,"why":"That is ±2σ."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"81.5%","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-037","group":"A12-S3-037","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Median of a cosine density","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=\\cos x$ for $0\\le x\\le\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$. Find the median.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.5235987755982989},"answerPrefix":"m =","hints":["Integrate cos x from 0 to m.","Set equal to ½.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate cos x from 0 to m.","method":"Set equal to ½.","worked":"$\\sin m=\\tfrac12$"},"steps":[{"h":"Area to m","d":"$\\sin m=\\tfrac12$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$m=\\tfrac{\\pi}{6}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.7853981633974483,"why":"The density is not symmetric.","expr":"pi/4"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"sin m = ½","line":"sin(m) = 1/2"},{"marks":1,"point":"π/6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-039","group":"A12-S3-039","dp":"S3.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Upper half of a linear density","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=\\tfrac x8$ for $0\\le x\\le4$. Find $P(X>2)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.75},"hints":["Integrate from 2 to 4.","Primitive x²/16.","Evaluate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate from 2 to 4.","method":"Primitive x²/16.","worked":"Evaluate."},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\left[\\tfrac{x^{2}}{16}\\right]_2^4=1-\\tfrac14$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"The density is not uniform.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3/4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-040","group":"A12-S3-040","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Median of a linear density","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=\\tfrac x8$ for $0\\le x\\le4$. Find the exact median.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2.8284271247461903},"answerPrefix":"m =","hints":["Area from 0 to m is ½.","Solve for m.","Positive root."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Area from 0 to m is ½.","method":"Solve for m.","worked":"$\\tfrac{m^{2}}{16}=\\tfrac12$"},"steps":[{"h":"Equation","d":"$\\tfrac{m^{2}}{16}=\\tfrac12$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$m^{2}=8$"}],"traps":[{"value":2,"why":"The density is not symmetric."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"m²/16 = ½","line":"m^2/16 = 1/2"},{"marks":1,"point":"2√2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-041","group":"A12-S3-041","dp":"S3.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":2,"title":"One below to two above","prompt":"$X\\sim N(60,4^{2})$. Use the empirical rule to find $P(56<X<68)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":81.5},"hints":["Standardise both.","Half of 68 plus half of 95.","Add."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Standardise both.","method":"Half of 68 plus half of 95.","worked":"$-1$ and $2$"},"steps":[{"h":"z-scores","d":"$-1$ and $2$"},{"h":"Rule","d":"$34+47.5$"}],"traps":[{"value":95,"why":"Treated both as 2 SD."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = −1 and 2","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"81.5%","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-042","group":"A12-S3-042","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tail from a table value","prompt":"$X\\sim N(50,10^{2})$. Given $P(Z<0.5)=0.6915$, find $P(X>55)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3085},"hints":["Standardise.","Use the complement.","Subtract."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Standardise.","method":"Use the complement.","worked":"$\\tfrac{55-50}{10}=0.5$"},"steps":[{"h":"z","d":"$\\tfrac{55-50}{10}=0.5$"},{"h":"Tail","d":"$1-0.6915$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.6915,"why":"That is P(X < 55)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = 0.5","line":"z = 0.5"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.3085","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-043","group":"A12-S3-043","dp":"S3.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Value from a z-score","prompt":"A data set has mean $40$ and standard deviation $6$. Which value has $z$-score $-1.5$?","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":31},"hints":["x = μ + zσ.","z is negative.","Evaluate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"x = μ + zσ.","method":"z is negative.","worked":"Evaluate."},"steps":[{"h":"Unstandardise","d":"$40-1.5\\times6$"}],"traps":[{"value":49,"why":"Sign of z."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"31","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-046","group":"A12-S3-046","dp":"S3.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Mode of a quadratic density","prompt":"$X$ has density $f(x)=6x(1-x)$ for $0\\le x\\le1$. Find the mode.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.5},"hints":["The mode is where f is largest.","Differentiate.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"The mode is where f is largest.","method":"Differentiate.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Maximum","d":"$f'(x)=6-12x=0$"}],"traps":[{"value":1.5,"why":"That is f(½).","expr":"3/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"½","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-048","group":"A12-S3-048","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Constant for a cubic density","prompt":"Find $k$ so that $f(x)=kx^{3}$ for $0\\le x\\le2$ (and $0$ elsewhere) is a probability density function.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.25},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Total area is 1.","∫₀² x³ dx = 4.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total area is 1.","method":"∫₀² x³ dx = 4.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Total area","d":"$k\\cdot\\tfrac{16}{4}=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.125,"why":"∫x³ = x⁴/4 gives 4.","expr":"1/8"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"k = 1/4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-049","group":"A12-S3-049","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Probability between two values of a density","prompt":"Using $f(x)=\\tfrac14x^{3}$ on $0\\le x\\le2$, find $P(X\\le1)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.0625},"hints":["Integrate from 0 to 1.","Primitive x⁴/16.","Evaluate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate from 0 to 1.","method":"Primitive x⁴/16.","worked":"Evaluate."},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\tfrac14\\cdot\\tfrac14$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.25,"why":"That is f(1).","expr":"1/4"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1/16","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-050","group":"A12-S3-050","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Mark from a percentile","prompt":"Exam marks are normal with mean $65$ and SD $10$. Given $P(Z<1.28)=0.90$, find the mark that cuts off the top $10\\%$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":77.8},"hints":["Top 10% means z = 1.28.","x = μ + zσ.","Compute."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Top 10% means z = 1.28.","method":"x = μ + zσ.","worked":"Compute."},"steps":[{"h":"Unstandardise","d":"$65+1.28\\times10$"}],"traps":[{"value":52.2,"why":"That is the bottom 10%."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"77.8","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-051","group":"A12-S3-051","dp":"S3.1c","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Median of a uniform density","prompt":"$X$ is uniformly distributed on $[2,10]$. Find $P(X<5)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.375},"hints":["Density 1/8.","Length from 2 to 5.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Density 1/8.","method":"Length from 2 to 5.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"Length ratio","d":"$\\tfrac{5-2}{8}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"The interval starts at 2.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3/8","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-055","group":"A12-S3-055","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Exponential density probability","prompt":"Waiting times have density $f(t)=0.5e^{-0.5t}$ for $t\\ge0$. Find $P(T>2)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.36787944117144233},"hints":["Integrate from 2 to ∞.","Primitive −e^{−0.5t}.","Evaluate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate from 2 to ∞.","method":"Primitive −e^{−0.5t}.","worked":"Evaluate."},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\left[-e^{-0.5t}\\right]_2^{\\infty}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.6321,"why":"That is P(T < 2)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"e⁻¹","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-057","group":"A12-S3-057","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Probability density on a symmetric interval","prompt":"A density is $f(x)=\\tfrac34(1-x^{2})$ for $-1\\le x\\le1$. Find $P(X>\\tfrac12)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.15625},"hints":["Integrate from ½ to 1.","Primitive x − x³/3.","Multiply by ¾."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Integrate from ½ to 1.","method":"Primitive x − x³/3.","worked":"$\\tfrac34\\left[x-\\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}\\right]_{1/2}^{1}$"},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\tfrac34\\left[x-\\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}\\right]_{1/2}^{1}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$\\tfrac34\\left(\\tfrac23-\\tfrac{11}{24}\\right)$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"Not half: the density is not uniform.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct integral","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"5/32","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-058","group":"A12-S3-058","dp":"S3.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Finding a standard deviation from a percentage","prompt":"A normal variable has mean $50$ and $16\\%$ of values exceed $58$. Using the empirical rule, find the standard deviation.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":8},"hints":["50 − 34 = 16%.","So 58 is 1 SD above."],"ladder":{"nudge":"50 − 34 = 16%.","method":"So 58 is 1 SD above.","worked":"Empirical"},"steps":[{"h":"Empirical","d":"$16\\%$ above means $z=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"16% is one SD, not two."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"8","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-059","group":"A12-S3-059","dp":"S3.1b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Expected value of a continuous variable","prompt":"Find $E(X)$ for $f(x)=\\tfrac38x^{2}$ on $0\\le x\\le2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":1.5},"hints":["E(X) = ∫x f(x) dx.","x⁴/4 from 0 to 2.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"E(X) = ∫x f(x) dx.","method":"x⁴/4 from 0 to 2.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"Integrate","d":"$\\int_0^2\\tfrac38x^{3}dx=\\tfrac38\\cdot4$"}],"traps":[{"value":1,"why":"That is the midpoint, not the mean."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3/2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-060","group":"A12-S3-060","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Between two z-scores from a table","prompt":"Given $P(Z<0.5)=0.6915$ and $P(Z<1.5)=0.9332$, find $P(0.5<Z<1.5)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.2417},"hints":["P(Z < 1.5) − P(Z < 0.5).","Subtract.","Done."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(Z < 1.5) − P(Z < 0.5).","method":"Subtract.","worked":"Done."},"steps":[{"h":"Subtract","d":"$0.9332-0.6915$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.6247,"why":"Subtract, do not add."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.2417","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-061","group":"A12-S3-061","dp":"S3.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Normal probability between mean and a value","prompt":"Using $P(Z<1)=0.8413$, find $P(0<Z<1)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3413},"hints":["P(Z < 0) = 0.5.","Subtract.","Done."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(Z < 0) = 0.5.","method":"Subtract.","worked":"Done."},"steps":[{"h":"Subtract","d":"$0.8413-0.5$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.8413,"why":"Subtract the left half."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.3413","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-062","group":"A12-S3-062","dp":"S3.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Constant for a sine density","prompt":"Find $k$ so that $f(x)=k\\sin x$ for $0\\le x\\le\\pi$ is a probability density.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.5},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Total area 1.","∫₀^π sin x dx = 2.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total area 1.","method":"∫₀^π sin x dx = 2.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Area","d":"$2k=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":1,"why":"∫sin from 0 to π is 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"½","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-063","group":"A12-S3-063","dp":"S3.1b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Median of an exponential density","prompt":"Find the median of $f(x)=2e^{-2x}$, $x\\ge0$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"ln(2)/2"},"answerPrefix":"m =","hints":["F(m) = ½.","Solve the exponential.","Take ln."],"ladder":{"nudge":"F(m) = ½.","method":"Solve the exponential.","worked":"Take ln."},"steps":[{"h":"CDF","d":"$1-e^{-2m}=\\tfrac12$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"ln(2)","why":"Divide by 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"CDF equation","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"(ln 2)/2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-069","group":"A12-S3-069","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Percentile from a z value","prompt":"Given $P(Z<0.84)=0.80$, find the $80$th percentile of $X\\sim N(60,25)$ (variance $25$).","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":64.2},"hints":["σ = √25 = 5.","x = μ + zσ.","Compute."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = √25 = 5.","method":"x = μ + zσ.","worked":"Compute."},"steps":[{"h":"Unstandardise","d":"$60+0.84\\times5$"}],"traps":[{"value":81,"why":"Use σ = 5, not σ² = 25."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"64.2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-077","group":"A12-S3-077","dp":"S3.1c","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Median of an exponential waiting time","prompt":"Waiting times have density $f(t)=\\tfrac15e^{-t/5}$. Find the median waiting time exactly.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"5*ln(2)"},"answerPrefix":"m =","hints":["F(m) = ½.","e^{−m/5} = ½.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"F(m) = ½.","method":"e^{−m/5} = ½.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"CDF","d":"$1-e^{-m/5}=\\tfrac12$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"5","why":"That is the mean."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"5 ln 2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-079","group":"A12-S3-079","dp":"S3.1c","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Uniform probability between bounds","prompt":"A bus arrives uniformly between $0$ and $15$ minutes. Find the probability you wait more than $10$ minutes.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3333333333333333},"hints":["Uniform.","Length 5 of 15.","Divide."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Uniform.","method":"Length 5 of 15.","worked":"Divide."},"steps":[{"h":"Length","d":"$\\tfrac{5}{15}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.6666666666666666,"why":"That is less than 10.","expr":"2/3"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"⅓","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-080","group":"A12-S3-080","dp":"S3.2b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Probability between two values with a table","prompt":"$X\\sim N(50,16)$. Given $P(Z<1.25)=0.8944$ and $P(Z<-0.5)=0.3085$, find $P(48<X<55)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.5859},"hints":["σ = 4.","z-scores.","Subtract."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = 4.","method":"z-scores.","worked":"$z=-0.5$ and $1.25$"},"steps":[{"h":"Standardise","d":"$z=-0.5$ and $1.25$"},{"h":"Subtract","d":"$0.8944-0.3085$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.2029,"why":"σ = 4, not 16."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Both z","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.5859","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-081","group":"A12-S3-081","dp":"S3.2b","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Finding the mean from a percentile","prompt":"$X$ is normal with SD $3$. $P(X>20)=0.1587$ and $P(Z<1)=0.8413$. Find the mean.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":17},"hints":["Upper tail 0.1587 means z = 1.","μ + σ = 20.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Upper tail 0.1587 means z = 1.","method":"μ + σ = 20.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"z","d":"$z=1$"},{"h":"Mean","d":"$20-3$"}],"traps":[{"value":23,"why":"20 is above the mean."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = 1","line":"1"},{"marks":1,"point":"17","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S3-085","group":"A12-S3-085","dp":"S3.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Piecewise density","prompt":"A density is $f(x)=\\tfrac x4$ for $0\\le x\\le2$ and $f(x)=c$ for $2<x\\le4$. Find $c$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.25},"answerPrefix":"c =","hints":["Triangle area ½.","Remaining ½.","Width 2."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Triangle area ½.","method":"Remaining ½.","worked":"$\\tfrac12$"},"steps":[{"h":"First part",